tion: Discarding J2 allows retention of potential melds in Dots (T4-T5-T6) and Characters (W3-W4-W6-W7) while minimizing points lost from discarded tile. Keeping F1 (Prevailing Wind) and J1 (Red Dragon) preserves opportunities for scoring patterns.\nReason: J2 is a non-essential tile with 3 remaining copies, reducing risk of aiding opponents. Retaining T4-T5-T6 supports potential concealed Chow, while F1 and J1 could contribute to Dragon Pung or Prevalent Wind scoring if completed later.\nAnswer: Play J2"}
